cker host gateway. |"],[167,"| Variable      | Default           | Notes                                        |\n| ------------- | ----------------- | -------------------------------------------- |\n| `litellm_key` | `\"\"`, `sensitive` | Handed to the workspace as `LITELLM_API_KEY` |"],[175,"| Variable     | Default | Notes                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              |\n| ------------ | ------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `github_mcp` | `true`  | Wires the `github` MCP HTTP server into Grok's rendered `config.toml`. Its `Authorization` header names `$GH_TOKEN` and nothing else, so no token value is ever part of a template variable. Set `GITHUB_MCP=false` and re-push to drop the block. |"],[172,"| Variable   | Default                                                                                                                                                 | Notes                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                      |\n| ---------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `repo_url` | `\"\"` in `workspace`, `https://github.com/coder/coder` in `devcontainer` (Terraform); `.env.sample` `REPO_URL` overrides both to this stack's GitHub URL | Prefills the **Git repository** field. Both templates clone that URL on the first start; a later start leaves a folder that already holds a `.git` alone. `REPO_URL` in `.env` overrides the default. The sample value is this stack's own repo so **VS Code Web** opens `~/workspace/evo-t1-coder-stack`. |"],[165,"| Variable | Default             | Notes                                                                                                                       |\n| -------- | ------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `image`  | `evo-t1-dev:latest` | Seeds the **Workspace image** dropdown default. In `devcontainer` it decides nothing about the toolchain inside the editor. |"],[171,"| Variable | Default | Notes                                                                                           |\n| -------- | ------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `dind`   | `false` | Turns on the per-workspace privileged daemon described below. Does not exist in `devcontainer`. |"],[700,"1 and 2 are the Coder agent's *default* discovery paths."],[701,"3 and 4 are the same text under the Grok Build CLI's convention, and the CLI is\nwhat `execute`-lane delegation drives. The chat agent dedupes skills by name,\nfirst match wins, home scope before a working-dir path, so one agent never loads a\nskill twice: the twins exist for the CLI, not as a second source for chat."],[268,"A **GitHub reauth** external app (`order = 7`, `/icon/github.svg`) opens Coder's\n`/external-auth/<id>` page in a slim window on the user's Coder session: connect, or\n**Reauthenticate** when the account is already linked. It stays on the main agent so\na failed clone (or a `devcontainer` subagent that never starts) still leaves the\nbutton on the workspace page. Device-flow login is not the App install: with the\ninjected App (id `github`) that page prints \"You must install the GitHub App to\nclone private repositories\" as unlinked plaintext, because Coder omits\n`AppInstallURL` on the default provider."],[271,"A **LiteLLM** tile (`/health/liveliness`, `share = \"owner\"`) that health-checks the\nproxy and is visible only to the workspace owner, plus a **Coder** external app."],[1182,"A `404` is what this stack answers for an unknown app slug or an agent that is not\nConnected; the agent is the text after the first `.` in `<ws>.<agent>`."],[142,"A `DEV_IMAGE` that is not in the local image store is a note, not a stop: build it\nfirst with `bazelisk run //scripts:build-dev-image`."],[23,"A `fix/…` branch that also has to rename a template directory, retarget a `.bats` suite, and\nupdate `docs/` is one change: the rename is not green until the last reference follows.\nWhen a rename cannot be proven complete, the reference stays (a rename is only \"done\" when\nthe old name is gone outside historical docs) and the CI file says so in a comment."],[182,"A `github_mcp` of `true` with no GitHub account connected gives that workspace a server\nthat fails its handshake once per session. A `context7_mcp` of `true` with an empty\n`context7_api_key` is the same shape: the block renders, and the server fails its\nhandshake once per session. Both are the pushed default now, so that shape is what a\nfresh deploy gets — `CONTEXT7_API_KEY` is optional and nothing in git carries a key.\nPark either one with `GITHUB_MCP=false` / `CONTEXT7_MCP=false` in `.env` and re-push."],[186,"A 0 default TTL leaves the checkbox unchecked and leaves `coder create` with nothing to\ninherit, so a workspace runs until its owner stops it."],[764,"A bind-mounted skill needs no recreate when the agent reloads skills from disk; start a\n**new Chat session** and the new skill is offered. Recreate only if it still does not\nshow up, since `restart` keeps the old mounts."],[677,"A built dev container mounts neither the volume nor the symlink, so it is the one\nplace the seed is **merged** instead of linked: the inlined\n`coder_script.code_server` fork bakes a base64 copy of it and writes it over the\ndev container's private `User/settings.json` (or merges over a copy that survived a\nrebuild, when `jq` is on PATH; without `jq` the existing file is kept). Edits\ninside a built dev container therefore survive neither a rebuild nor a look at the\nshared file. Everywhere else no settings map is passed at all, because a merge\nwould replace the symlink."],[282,"A built dev container sees neither the volume nor that symlink, so it is the one place\nthe seed is merged instead of linked."],[908,"A busy pinned box sheds its own overflow in its own scheduler instead of queueing\ninside the proxy."],[564,"A card per service, with status pulled from each service's own API over the compose\nnetwork - `http://coder:3000`, `http://litellm:4000`, `http://ollama:11434`,\n`http://hermes:9119/api/status` - so nothing here needs a daemon credential. The\nheader carries boxed tiles for host CPU, memory, CPU temperature, disk and `eth0`\nthroughput, beside the clock, local weather (open-meteo, keyless) and a DuckDuckGo\nsearch."],[1155,"A chat that starts but narrates instead of calling tools is the no-Spark case above."],[687,"A chat turn needs an enabled chat model config - the chat's own pick, else the\ndeployment default, else it errors before the first tool call - and that wiring is\nwhat the script writes. It mints a short-lived admin API token from the stack's own\nPostgres (`token_name 'stack-coder-agents'`, deleted by the trap, never printed) and\ndrives the server's experimental chat API:"],[1134,"A checkout that does not yet contain that `--repair` (the usual case: `git pull`\nis already failing) needs the same commands by hand, then pull:"],[1049,"a Coder certificate whose DNS SANs now carry the public names alongside the existing\nones. The LAN cert keeps working; in public mode the browser never sees it, since\nTraefik presents real ones."],[907,"A conversation that goes quiet for longer than the TTL may move."],[903,"A cooled box therefore stays visibly out of `healthy_deployments` instead of blending\ninto the group's aggregate stats."],[267,"A custom **Web Terminal** command-app at `order = 6` takes the terminal slot. Custom\napps are ordered among themselves; static helper buttons have no `order` or `icon` knob\nin this Coder release and are not reorderable."],[1170,"A declared context7 server that fails handshake: empty `CONTEXT7_API_KEY` is\nthe supported public-rate-limit shape. A key in `.env` plus a re-push fills\nthe env; the block still renders with no key."],[1169,"A declared github server that fails handshake: the owner has not connected\nGitHub External Auth, so `$GH_TOKEN` is empty. Use the **GitHub reauth** app,\nthen start a new Grok session."],[135,"A dev stack that moved the search port needs its own template push: `searxng_url`\nis derived from `STACK_SEARCH_PORT` as read from `.env`, so a push made while\n`dev-stack.env` carries `18181` still names `8181` unless the key is set in `.env`\ntoo. A workspace dials the host gateway, where the compose network does not help,\nso the port in the rendered `SEARXNG_URL` has to be the one actually published."],[1128,"A failed bind from an older runfiles compose file can also leave a **directory**\n(or a root-owned file) at `homepage/assets/icons/evo-t1.svg` inside\n`bazel-out/.../prod-stack.runfiles`. The next `bazelisk run` then dies before\nthe stack script starts; that spelling is the next heading."],[102,"A failed description edit and a failed autostop pin only add a note; neither blocks the\ntemplate."],[470,"A file carrying the stack marker — `managed-by: evo-t1-coder-stack`, or the\n`\"__evoT1Stack\": true` key — is stack-owned and is reseeded when the seed in this repo\ndrifted."],[595,"A GMKtec EVO-T1 (or any box with the Arc 140T and enough RAM for the model in\n`OLLAMA_MODELS`) with Docker and Compose v2 installed."],[1174,"A hit in the first means Coder tried the upstream and gave up, so the fault sits on\nthis box: check the devcontainer or workspace container first, then `DOCKER_HOST`."],[1257,"A manual PAT is legitimate in two cases: the workspace owner connected no Coder\naccount, so nothing can be minted, or the minted/App credential is missing the\nrepository - revoked or expired counts the same way, because the answer that proves\neither is NOT VISIBLE or REJECTED, not a passing read. It REPLACES the per-start\nminted credential for that workspace, so treat it as a stand-in and rotate or remove\nit in GitHub -> Applications when the work ends."],[471,"A marker-free file is user-owned and stays untouched unless `--force` says otherwise.\nThe terminal helpers and `notes-setup.sh` are the exception: startup rewrites those on\nevery boot, so this script does too."],[1168,"A missing `[mcp_servers.github]` or `[mcp_servers.context7]` in\n`~/.grok/config.toml` means the last push passed `--var …=false`, or the\nworkspace started from an older template. Re-push and restart the workspace\nso the managed `config.toml` re-renders."],[140,"A missing `docker`, `timeout`, `tar` or `openssl`, a stack that is not running, or no\nactive Coder account is a *skip*: a one-line reason and exit 0. `bootstrap.sh` calls\nthis script, and a fresh clone has none of those prerequisites yet."],[205,"A missing image fails the workspace build at **plan** time, before anything is\ncreated, with `did not find docker image 'docker:29.8.1-dind'` - see\ntroubleshooting.md."],[529,"A native `bazelisk test` on macOS is convenience only: the BSD userland differs from the\nGNU one in the image (`sed`, `date`, `find`, `sort`), so a red run there is not proof of a\ndefect and a green one is not the run that unlocks the merge button. CI and branch\nprotection gate on the image result either way."],[1258,"A PAT is never typed as an argument any more: argv is readable through `ps` and the\ntoken lands in shell history. Pipe it in (`echo \"$TOKEN\" | bazelisk run\n//scripts:github-auth -- auth <container> -`) or run `auth <container>` alone and\nanswer the hidden prompt. In the line above, `-` is the only argument after the\ncontainer and `< PAT` is a shell redirect, not an argument."],[315,"A PAT is never typed as an argument any more. `auth <container> <PAT>` is refused\nbecause argv is readable through `ps` and lands in shell history, so the script takes\nthe token on stdin only: pipe it in (`echo \"$TOKEN\" | bazelisk run\n//scripts:github-auth -- auth <container> -`) or run `auth <container>` alone and\nanswer the hidden prompt."],[253,"A persistent per-workspace home volume (`coder-<wsid>-home`)."],[572,"A plain `restart` keeps the generated page, so day-to-day YAML edits need nothing.\nNew asset files do need a recreate (`up -d`), since `restart` keeps the old mounts."],[298,"A private extra repository still has to be GRANTED to the connected GitHub account, or\nits clone is refused, just like the primary one."],[1000,"A probe-style CLI takes its target as a flag (`--url`) rather than a hard-coded host, and reports\n\"nothing answered\" as a result rather than a crash, so one run works from the host and from inside\na workspace and still answers the question the operator asked. Its suite stubs the transport."],[485,"A pull request that does not touch `images/dev/**` replays the cached layers instead of\nrebuilding them, which is what keeps the gate's wall time flat."],[120,"A push is also the only thing that *registers* a template: Coder stores the source as a\nFilestore row, not as files it scans on disk."],[862,"A rename or deletion is the edit that can reach workspaces: both\n`templates/*/grok-config.toml.tftpl` twins render the alias list into\n`~/.grok/config.toml`, a running workspace keeps the copy it rendered at start, and\nthe next start re-renders it."],[106,"A repeated name is one push, not two, and the push order stays `TEMPLATES_DEFAULT`\norder whatever the argument order is. Naming `devcontainer` first cannot orphan it."],[1242,"A repo that ships none wants the **Plain clone** preset, or the dev-container toggle\nset to **No** at create time. Either one runs code-server on the plain workspace\ncontainer and opens the clone there."],[222,"A repository that ships no `devcontainer.json` gets no dev container and hence no\neditor with the toggle on. The toggle - or\n`bazelisk run //scripts:new-workspace -- <git-url>`, which reads the repository and\npicks for you - is how that case is meant to be handled."],[888,"A request carrying `tools` for `qwen2.5-coder:32b` or `:14b` comes back as plain text,\n`finish_reason: \"stop\"`, and no `tool_calls` field at all."],[1059,"A router per name pointing at `http://<this-box-lan-ip>:8080`, including\n`hermes-gmktecbeast.overeazy.io`. That backend is `:8080` with the original Host,\nthe same as the other four - not `:9119`. A router aimed at `:9119` skips this\nbox's vhost. The file in Traefik configuration is that\nconfig; diff what the box runs against it."],[542,"A script must work when the cwd is **not** the checkout. Under `bazel test` the working\ndirectory is an exec root or a runfiles tree that holds *copies* of whatever the target\ndeclares as `data`; under `bazel run` it is wherever the operator typed `bazelisk`, and\n`bazel run` alone sets `BUILD_WORKSPACE_DIRECTORY`. Neither guarantees a working Docker\ndaemon, an `ssh`, or a reachable Spark box — a sandboxed action usually has none of them on\nPATH."],[998,"A script never runs another repo script by relative path, and never assumes the cwd is the\ncheckout: it resolves the repo root from `${REPO_ROOT:-}` / `${GITHUB_WORKSPACE:-}` and then\nprobes for it (see the harness doc), because a Bazel sandbox may only hold a copy."],[649,"A self-installed CLI under `~/.grok/bin` stays first on the login-shell PATH, so it\nwins over the baked copy."],[266,"A separate in-browser **code-server** editor is Coder's VS Code fork (no local VS\nCode), labelled **VS Code Web** with `order = 5` so it sorts before GitHub reauth (7),\nInstall GitHub App (8), LiteLLM (10) and Coder UI (11) and reads apart from the\n**VS Code Desktop** helper."],[937,"A single conversation pinned to one box now keeps its streams on that box while it\nstays healthy - that is the behaviour the burst predates."],[763,"A skill is one directory: `hermes/skills/<name>/SKILL.md`, with\nagentskills.io frontmatter for the name and description.\nCommit it, and the next `up` has it."],[525,"A suite is one cached action. Its `.bats` file, `test_helper.bash`, `test_helpers.sh`,\n`bats_runner.sh` and the `scripts/**.sh` plus stub/fixture files it declares as `data` are\nits inputs, so editing one script re-runs only the suites that read it, and an unchanged\nsuite replays its cached PASS."],[103,"A template whose push or verification failed is counted in the\n`N of M template(s) did not reach an active version` line and makes the run exit\nnon-zero, while every other template still gets its push attempt."],[691,"a three-line system-prompt addendum, appended after Coder's default prompt text\n(`include_default_system_prompt: true`), that keeps the delegation and\nsecret-hygiene rules which must hold even when a chat has no workspace attached."],[307,"A token that authenticates but was never GRANTED the repository still fails clone and\npush, and reads prove nothing about write: a private repository hidden from the\ncredential answers 403 or 404 on both lanes, and a public one answers a read probe\nwith 200 for any authenticated caller, so a read-only credential passes a read test\nwhile every write to that repo is denied.\n`bazelisk run //scripts:github-auth -- check <repo-url>` asks the write question\ndirectly: one GET of\n`<repo>.git/info/refs?service=git-receive-pack`, the endpoint `git push` itself\nnegotiates through."],[240,"A tracked `.devcontainer/contributor-env` outranks every other signal: the probe is a\n**miss** even when the same clone also tracks `.devcontainer/devcontainer.json`. That is\nhow this repo keeps its own Coder workspaces on `workspace` — the `.devcontainer/` it\nships is the contributor one for a laptop and CI, not a nested toolchain to rebuild\ninside the workspace's own DinD sidecar (see\ncontribute/devcontainer.md). Application repositories do\nnot carry the sentinel, so their dev containers stay a hit."],[910,"A value has to look like an id to count: alphanumerics, hyphens or underscores, 8\ncharacters or more. The sources, in order, are `x-litellm-trace-id`, then\n`x-litellm-session-id`, then any `x-<vendor>-session-id`, then\n`session-id`/`session_id`/`thread-id`/`conversation_id` (Codex style), then W3C\ntraceparent and baggage, plus `metadata.session_id` in the body."],[1043,"A wildcard certificate covers exactly one label, so the dotted two-label form\n(`coder.gmktecbeast.`) has no certificate at the public edge: the browser aborts with\n`ERR_SSL_VERSION_OR_CIPHER_MISMATCH` and Traefik never sees the request. Measured on\nthis box - `coder-gmktecbeast.overeazy.io` completes the handshake with the zone's\n`*.overeazy.io` cert, while the dotted form fails with a TLS alert 40 and presents\nno certificate at all."],[592,"A working stack on a fresh box without reading the whole README first"],[1034,"A workspace **app** link (the **LiteLLM** and **Open VS Code Web** buttons) rides the\ncoder row of that table. Both `coder_app` blocks set `subdomain = false`, so their\nURL keeps the `/@<owner>/<ws>.<agent>/apps/<slug>` path form and goes to `coder:3000`\non its way to `host.docker.internal:4000`. A 502 on that link is an app-lane failure\nand `litellm-gmktecbeast.` took no part in it."],[1082,"A workspace app link answers `Bad Gateway` -> find who answered"],[373,"A workspace moving `shared` -> `private` starts on an empty profile: nothing is\ncopied and the shared volume is left alone."],[247,"A workspace name can follow the URL. Coder names start with a letter (40 characters\nmax); the derived default is the repository leaf."],[189,"A workspace owner can still tick the box for one workspace: `allow_user_autostop`\nstays on, because CE cannot turn it off -- `--allow-user-autostop=false` is marked\n\"can only be disabled in enterprise\"."],[932,"A wrong model id does not crash the proxy: 1.102.1 builds the Router with\n`ignore_invalid_deployments` forced to True, so a bad id drops that deployment at boot\nwith one log line and later surfaces as \"No deployments available\"."],[710,"Access"],[402,"Adding a script without editing a BUILD file"],[511,"Adding a test that passes in the Bazel sandbox and on a laptop"],[553,"After a recreate: revalidate once"],[893,"Agent mode therefore needs either the Spark `agent` lane or the small `chat` model."],[1162,"Agent traffic ignores that URL and dials `host.docker.internal:3002`; see the\n`coder_agent_url` template variable."],[269,"An **Install GitHub App** external app (`order = 8`, same icon, opens in a tab)\nis the clickable install path for that default App:\n`https://github.com/apps/coder/installations/new`. It is declared only while\n`github_auth_id` is `github`. After installing, grant the private repos the\nworkspace clones, then restart so `GH_TOKEN` remints."],[688,"an `openai-compat` AI provider named **`litellm`** (not `litellm-auto`), base URL\n`http://litellm:4000/v1` - LiteLLM over the compose network, *server-side*,\nauthenticated with `LITELLM_MASTER_KEY`. The agent dials the in-process AI Gateway\n(aibridge), which forwards to the provider's `base_url` + `/chat/completions`, so\n`/v1` has to be part of the base URL and the key has to match the live proxy: with\n`.env` leaving the key empty, compose still boots the proxy on its\n`change-me-litellm` interpolation default, and that default is what gets sent.\nCreated when absent, drift-patched when an existing provider carries a drifted\n`base_url` or key."],[301,"An `ssh://` or `git@` URL reaches nothing here - this stack provisions no SSH keys."],[860,"An alias is a `model_name:` entry in `litellm/config.yaml`, not a model."],[210,"An always-on privileged `docker:29.8.1-dind` sidecar on the per-workspace bridge\nnetwork, with `DOCKER_HOST=tcp://dind:2375` injected **unconditionally** and\n`DOCKER_TLS_CERTDIR=` empty for the reasons above. `internal` stays false for the same\none reason."],[672,"An empty result page and \"no answer\" are different answers, which is why the probe\nreports which one it got."],[1048,"an extended `HOMEPAGE_ALLOWED_HOSTS` - homepage validates the incoming Host against\nthat exact-match list, so an unlisted name fails its host check;"],[297,"An extra folder never becomes the folder the tools open on: the editor, the Web\nTerminal button and the tmux helpers all stay on the primary clone."],[1047,"an upgraded `CODER_ACCESS_URL` (the public coder name);"],[1061,"Any authentication as the Traefik router's middleware. Authelia already fronts\n`hermes-gmktecbeast.overeazy.io` (the name 302s), the same interactive policy as\nthe homepage and Coder names. The sidecar forwards what it receives and\nauthenticates nothing, so a name whose router skips the auth middleware reaches\nits container the same way the LAN does. The app path is behind that policy\nlike the rest of its name, so an expired session surfaces there too."],[1267,"Anything else means the router matched (Hermes basic auth is `401` until you\nsend credentials). A `421` only on the public URL, with this probe succeeding,\nis a rewritten Host or a Traefik backend that is not `:8080`."],[685,"Apply it (or re-run after a skip):"],[722,"Approval prompts, bootstrap seeding, and the skills directory"],[714,"Approvals"],[31,"Argument handling"],[105,"Arguments are template *names*, and they select which names to push. A name that is not\none of the known names is an error that lists the known names, so a typo cannot quietly\ndo nothing."],[541,"Assertions come from `tests/test_helpers.sh`: `fail`, `assert_eq`, `assert_match`,\n`assert_not_match`, `assert_file_exists`, `assert_file_not_exists`, `load_shell_function`.\n`load_shell_function` is the one harness place that expands a function body (it is how a\nsingle entry-CLI function gets unit-tested); production scripts still never use `eval`."],[711,"Auth"],[1018,"Authelia"],[183,"Autostart, autostop and TTLs are template *metadata*, so they stay out of the Terraform\n(where they would fight the UI) and travel on the CLI after pushing."],[40,"Autostop and TTLs"],[151,"Autostop is metadata, not Terraform. Re-pin it with `templates edit` after a push made\nfrom the checkout root, or on the dev stack swap `-p evo-t1-coder-stack` for\n`-p evo-t1-dev --env-file dev-stack.env`."],[62,"Autostop, TTLs, Docker-in-Docker, and the DinD sidecar failure modes"],[694,"Backgrounded and polled because `execute` waits only a short window per tool call\n(about a minute), so a synchronous foreground `grok -p` would die mid-run on any big\ntask. Coder Agents then reviews the delegated diff, runs the project's tests, and\ncommits. Subagents spawned by Coder Agents cannot create workspaces: provisioning\ndecisions stop at the top-level chat."],[646,"Baked in at `/usr/local/bin/grok`, with an `agent` link beside it, **outside** the\n`/home/coder` home volume, so a rebuilt volume cannot lose it."],[390,"Bazelisk as the ingress for tests, lint and the operator CLIs, and what the runfiles layout means for a script you just added."],[404,"Bazelisk is how this repo runs tests, lint, and the operator CLIs. The Makefile targets call\nthe same commands. test-with-bazel.md covers the Bats harness;\n../branching.md the branch rules that CI guards;\ndevcontainer.md the container that carries the toolchain."],[992,"Bazelisk is the only ingress, with one exception: `scripts/setup-host.sh`. That script is\nthe **stack host's** bootstrap — it installs Bazelisk, the shell/Starlark lint toolchain\n(shellcheck, shfmt, buildifier) and Terraform — so it has to run before Bazel exists, and\nstays the single documented `bash scripts/setup-host.sh`. On a laptop you do not run it:\nthe contributor container or `bazelisk run //scripts:test-in-image` brings the same pinned\ntoolchain in from `images/dev/` instead\n(contribute/devcontainer.md). `--repair` is the other half of\nthat exemption: leftover Docker bind-mounts in Bazel's runfiles tree make\n`bazelisk run //scripts:prod-stack` die creating `prod-stack.runfiles` (`Permission\ndenied` on `homepage/assets/icons/evo-t1.svg`) before any stack script can run.\nOn Linux it also writes a systemd-resolved drop-in (`1.1.1.1` / `8.8.8.8`) and\nruns `tailscale set --accept-dns=false` so host `git pull` still resolves\n`github.com` when MagicDNS is the only nameserver."],[957,"Before you reach for a hammer"],[584,"Before you start"],[19,"Below the subject leave one empty line, then the bullet points, and leave an empty line\nbetween every two bullets, so each bullet is its own paragraph. The same rule is in\n`templates/common/GROK_BUILD_AGENTS.md`, which is the text every workspace seeds into\n`~/.grok/AGENTS.md`, so a commit written by an agent and one written by hand read the\nsame way in `git log`."],[715,"Bootstrap and skills"],[773,"Bootstrap options, including `--data` and `--force`:"],[598,"Bootstrap the toolchain — the only step that runs before Bazel exists, because it is what\ninstalls Bazelisk:"],[704,"Both `main.tf` files deliberately set **no** `CODER_AGENT_EXP_*` env keys on\n`coder_agent.main`: those keys *replace* the agent's discovery defaults, and the\ndefaults already cover exactly the seeded paths - the `~/.coder` roots plus a\nworking-dir-relative `.agents/skills`, which resolves inside the agent's working\ndir (`/home/coder` in `workspace`; in `devcontainer` with the toggle on, the\ncloned folder under `/srv/coder-devcontainers/...`, where a dev container built on\nthe sidecar carries its own home and no seeded path is visible from inside it\nanyway)."],[858,"Both doors authenticate with the same `LITELLM_MASTER_KEY` value."],[916,"Both float across the healthy boxes by load."],[408,"Both give you the GNU userland the gate runs on, which a macOS laptop cannot promise\nnatively. Neither replaces the bootstrap below — that one is for the stack host."],[1188,"Both of these answer nothing in that case; the first is the one to type:"],[101,"Both the preset descriptions and the two routing hints fit the same 128-byte ceiling.\n`coder_parameter` descriptions are **not** capped (some run past 450 characters) and are\nnot checked."],[276,"Both twins' `coder_app` opens on `http://localhost:13337/?folder=<urlencoded>`. The\n`coder_app` resource in `coder/coder` `~> 2.18` has no `folder` argument, so the\nfolder rides in the URL, in the Web Terminal's `command`, and as a positional\nargument to the code-server binary with `--ignore-last-opened` (path-based apps\ndrop the query string, and without that flag the last restored workspace wins)."],[912,"Both workspace templates render `x-litellm-session-id = \"ws-<workspace-uuid>\"` under\n`[models]` in `~/.grok/config.toml`, so one key covers every conversation of a\nworkspace, subagent calls included."],[21,"Branch protection on `main` should require a pull request before pushing, and the two\nBazel checks before merging — `//:test-fast` and `//:lint`, run inside the golden image\nthe workflow builds, so a green check means the suite passed on the Linux toolchain the\nstack actually ships rather than on whatever the runner image carried that day."],[1,"Branching"],[1148,"Bring the TensorFold server up on the box. `<host>` is what `.env` names, and `--apply`\nwrites the per-host override file that server runs:"],[332,"Bringing an old checkout back to a runnable state with one command"],[589,"Bringing the stable stack up and pulling the models"],[1105,"Browser editor (code-server) stays unhealthy -> check these three, in order"],[451,"Build it locally when you want the tag in the local store (the Coder docker provider\nresolves `evo-t1-dev:latest` from there and never pulls):"],[389,"Building with Bazel"],[1230,"Builds still succeed, so verify with a workspace build before acting on it. Nothing\nin this repo's compose file sets the provisioner's Terraform."],[565,"Card `href`s come from `STACK_CODER_URL` / `STACK_KASM_URL` / `STACK_LITELLM_URL` /\n`STACK_HERMES_URL`, which default to LAN URLs built from `STACK_LAN_HOST` and the\nport variables. Change a port or re-detect the LAN IP and the links follow; set\n`STACK_PUBLIC_HOSTS` and the cards follow the public names. The Hermes card\nfollows `STACK_HERMES_URL` when bootstrap sets it, and stays on\n`http://<STACK_LAN_HOST>:9119` when that key is empty. See hermes.md."],[1132,"Cause: `/etc/resolv.conf` names only Tailscale MagicDNS (`100.100.100.100`).\nDocker's iptables, and Kasm's privileged nested dockerd, can make that stub\nunreachable. When it is, **every** lookup dies, including `github.com`, so\n`git pull` over HTTPS fails. This is host DNS, not GitHub auth."],[1194,"Cause: `/learn` is a bundled user-invocable skill of Grok Build 1.0.70, not a\nterminal slash-command this repo seeds. Workspaces still running the previous\npin (1.0.44) have no bundled learn, and a self-installed `~/.grok/bin/grok` that\nsits first on PATH hides the image's copy."],[1219,"Cause: `bazelisk run` executes from the runfiles tree, where `templates/**` are\nsymlinks into the execroot. A tar that stores those links unpacks in the\nprovisioner as dangling paths, so Terraform sees no `.tf` files. The two\n`templates/common/` payloads still land (copied with `cp`, which follows\nlinks), which is why the archive is small rather than empty."],[1231,"Cause: `coder/preview` warns when a `coder_app` `count` is not expanded at\nworkspace-create preview. `start_count` is that value. The default is then\nassumed to be 1."],[1125,"Cause: `docker compose` resolved `./proxy/homepage.conf` (or another file bind\nmount) next to a compose file that did not have that file. Under `bazelisk run`\nthat file used to be the runfiles copy, which only holds `//:stack_data`. Docker\nthen created a directory at the source path and failed mounting it onto nginx's\n`/etc/nginx/conf.d/default.conf`, which is a file in the image."],[1185,"Cause: a pinned download returned an error. The layer prints `curl: (22)` and stops\nrather than shipping a partial image."],[1129,"Cause: an older `bazelisk run` used the runfiles copy of `docker-compose.yml`, so\ncompose mounted `./homepage/assets/icons` from `bazel-out`. Docker then created a\ndirectory where `evo-t1.svg` belongs, or the homepage container chowned those\nfiles to root. Bazel cannot recreate `prod-stack.runfiles` over that leftover,\nand the stack script never starts, so a repair inside `prod-stack` cannot help."],[1228,"Cause: an upstream pin. The Coder image ships its own provisioner binary at\n`/usr/local/bin/terraform` (1.15.5 in `coder:v2.36.6`) and Coder caps the version it\nwas tested against."],[1216,"Cause: both templates inline `templates/common/vscode-alt.svg` as a\n`data:image/svg+xml;base64` URL on `coder_app.code_server`. Coder v2.36 stores\n`workspace_apps.icon` as `varchar(256)`. A multi-kilobyte SVG produces a data\nURL thousands of characters long, and the insert fails. The provisioner\nreports it at `insert agent app: upsert app`."],[1233,"Cause: Coder runs every `coder_script` as `bash -c`. HCL heredocs in `main.tf` only\nescape `$${name}` to `${name}`; `$$((` is two literal dollars. The editor wait loop\nthen becomes `waited=<pid>((waited + 1))`, which is the syntax error. The echo\nbefore the loop still prints. `already cloned, skipping` on the next line is the\nconcurrent clone stage, not the failure."],[1200,"Cause: Docker creates an empty named volume as `root:root` 755. The\n`vscode-settings-<owner-id>` volume is empty on first use (the image has no\nfiles there to copy in), so `coder` cannot write `settings.json`. `jq` and\n`python` then fail because the file was never created. `already cloned, skipping`\non the next line is informational: the clone already exists."],[1259,"Cause: Hermes v0.22.5 refuses a non-loopback bind when no\n`DashboardAuthProvider` is registered. The bundled basic-auth plugin skips\nregistration when the password is empty. Compose interpolation\n`${HERMES_DASHBOARD_PASSWORD:-}` (empty default) did that after a pull that\nadded the Hermes keys: `.env` never gained them, so `prod-stack up` without\n`bootstrap` / `update-configs` crash-looped the gateway. The logs repeat\n\"no auth providers are registered\" and do not mention `plugins.disabled`."],[1142,"Cause: no Spark box was reachable, so the Arc answered, and the Arc path returns tool\ncalls as plain text."],[1235,"Cause: path-based Coder apps drop the `?folder=` query before the browser sees\nit, and code-server restores the last opened workspace (often `/home/coder`).\nThe clone itself is fine (`already cloned, skipping` is not a failure)."],[1212,"Cause: provisionerd runs `terraform init` inside the `coder` container.\nDocker's embedded DNS (`127.0.0.11`) forwards names it does not know to\nthe host resolver. When that resolver is Tailscale MagicDNS only, or\nDocker/Kasm iptables has made `100.100.100.100` unreachable from a\ncontainer, every public lookup SERVFAILs. The host CLI is fine; only the\nprovisioner job dies. The lockfile reuse lines (`Reusing previous version\nfrom the dependency lock file`) do not skip the registry: Terraform still\nfetches the discovery document."],[1152,"Cause: that chat has no model config on this deployment, so there is nothing to route to."],[1187,"Cause: that container started before the CLI was baked into the image, or its\nstart-time download failed."],[1198,"Cause: that container was built from an image predating the Docker client toolchain,\nor from the bare-Ubuntu *Minimal shell* preset."],[1208,"Cause: that image is not in the host's local image store, and Terraform never pulls\nit. The `docker_image` data source only inspects the store."],[1270,"Cause: the Chat tab is a WebSocket on `/api/pty` and `/api/ws`. Hermes sends a\nkeepalive every 20 seconds. Close code `4403` is the Host / Origin / peer guard."],[1224,"Cause: the CLI is talking to a public subdomain, and Authelia answers its API calls\nwith the sign-in page."],[1204,"Cause: the sidecar is unhealthy, its image was never pulled, or the workspace was\ncreated with DinD off."],[1264,"Cause: this box's `router` answers `421` when the Host matches no `server_name`.\nThe hermes vhost lives in `proxy/router.conf` (hardcoded, like the other public\nnames). Traefik pointed at `:9119` never hits that file. A rewritten Host also\nmisses every block."],[619,"Caveats, honestly"],[633,"Changing a model alias in one place and knowing which workspaces see it"],[66,"Changing a template variable without guessing which file owns it"],[663,"Changing the mode needs a **rebuild** - the nested mount either exists or it does\nnot. A workspace that goes from `shared` to `private` starts on an empty profile:\nnothing is copied, and the shared volume is left alone."],[689,"chat model configs `agent` (context limit 262144, set as the default; LiteLLM bakes\n`reasoning_effort` `xhigh`), `agent-low` / `agent-medium` / `agent-xhigh` (same\nlane with a baked thinking level, not default), and `chat` (32768), for models not\nalready registered. `coder` and `coder-fast` stay out on purpose: on this stack's\nIPEX-LLM runtime those weights return tool calls as plain text with no\n`tool_calls`, and an agent turn without callable tools cannot browse or edit, so\nregistering them would only add a silently broken model to the pickers.\n`context_limit` is the agent's own compaction budget (a 70 per cent default\ncompaction threshold applies), which is why it is pinned per alias."],[693,"Chat on the Agents page -> if the ask needs more tooling than chat has, Coder Agents\nprovisions or uses a workspace through `execute` -> big multi-file tasks are\n*delegated inside* that workspace: a headless Grok Build CLI run, started backgrounded\nand polled:"],[921,"Chat stays usable while agent mode quietly loses its tools. That is the point of the\nhop, not an accident."],[1112,"Chat tab never connects, or the socket closes `4403` -> public URL, trusted proxies, or a dropped Upgrade"],[1237,"Check 1: the code-server install script's log is green in the workspace's Scripts/Log\ntab."],[1238,"Check 2: this answers from inside the workspace:"],[1239,"Check 3: the browser is on `https://` with a trusted cert. Plain `http://` is an\ninsecure context, which is what breaks `crypto.randomUUID()`; see \"Public subdomains\n(optional)\" in README.md."],[154,"Check it in the Coder UI afterwards: **Default autostop** must read *Disabled* (0 h)."],[191,"Check it in the Coder UI: the template editor's **Default autostop** reads *Disabled*\n(0 h), and a workspace's **Schedule** tab shows **Enable Autostop** unchecked."],[940,"Check that `SPARK_1_API_KEY`, `SPARK_2_API_KEY` and `SPARK_3_API_KEY` are still\nnon-empty. An empty key fails every request inside the proxy, before it ever reaches\nthe box."],[1251,"Check the GitHub side first. The grant behind the credential - the GitHub App\ninstallation that the External Auth provider (id `github` by default) minted its token from -\nhas to include the repository the workspace clones or pushes. An empty\ngithub.com/settings/apps page is the usual surprise\nhere: it means no App is installed under your account, so there is no **Configure** link\nto click and nothing to grant, while the provider itself stays configured and keeps\nminting tokens that authenticate. Install Coder's App from the workspace **Install\nGitHub App** button, or at\ngithub.com/apps/coder/installations/new,\ngrant the repo, then restart. A private repository is never visible to a credential\nthat was never granted it."],[1017,"Checking the other machine"],[1024,"Checking the other machine (including the Hermes WebSocket), Authelia, and the two follow-ups left by hand"],[64,"Choosing between the plain container and the devcontainer before you click create"],[5,"CI and protection"],[20,"CI runs only for `push` to `main` and for `pull_request` targeting `main`."],[914,"Cline and Roo editor traffic carries no session id: the extension settings have no\ncustom-header field."],[676,"Cline and Roo/Kilo are pre-wired to the LiteLLM proxy (endpoint from `litellm_url`,\ndefault `http://host.docker.internal:4000/v1`; model alias `agent`, with\n`agent-low`/`agent-medium`/`agent-xhigh`/`coder`/`coder-fast`/`chat` listed in\n`__evoT1StackModels`). The seed is\n`settings.json.tftpl`, copied onto the per-owner volume\n`vscode-settings-<owner-id>` (mounted at `~/.shared/vscode/settings.json`) only\nwhile that file is absent, and symlinked from\n`~/.local/share/code-server/User/settings.json`. Startup chowns that volume to\nthe home owner before the first write (empty named volumes are `root:root`\n755). Edits stick, and every workspace\nthat owner has shares the file; delete it to copy the template in again. From the\nhost it is the volume's `settings.json`:"],[46,"Clone and build"],[56,"Cloning more than one repository"],[1030,"Cloudflare proxies the name (orange cloud) in front of Traefik. WebSockets are on\nthere by default, which is what the Hermes Chat tab needs."],[281,"code-server's User settings file is a symlink to that path, so every workspace that\nowner has opens the same file, and an edit - in any workspace, or from the host by\nmounting the volume - is not overwritten on the next start. Delete the file to reseed\nfrom the template."],[621,"Coder Agents (control-plane)"],[1078,"Coder Agents chat refuses every prompt, or its model dropdown is empty -> no model config"],[915,"Coder Agents chats carry none either. Coder's aibridge forwards model calls with the\nprovider key only and adds no per-conversation session id."],[707,"Coder Agents is control-plane-native. This stack does not wrap Grok Build: the wiring\nabove *teaches* (skill + instructions) and *equips* (the workspace-side CLI with its\nLiteLLM alias) the native Coder agent to drive Grok Build when work is too big to\nhand-drive. Delegation is a taught habit, not the product."],[632,"Coder Agents on the control plane and the model config it needs"],[1114,"Coder login problems -> the admin account, and `CODER_ACCESS_URL`"],[185,"Coder reads the template's **Default autostop** (its default TTL) when it seeds a\nworkspace. That field also decides whether the create form's **Enable Autostop**\narrives ticked, and it ships at 24 h - which is how a workspace would otherwise start\nwith a shutdown deadline nobody chose."],[679,"Coder v2.36.6 ships *Coder Agents*: a coding agent that lives in the Coder **server** -\na chat UI and an API beside your workspaces, not inside one. A chat runs its tools\n(`read_file`, `edit_files`, `execute`, `spawn_agent`) against a workspace over that\nworkspace's agent connection, and consults two pieces of per-workspace context first:\nan **instructions** file and any **skills** it discovers. The agent itself is upstream\nCoder, not a home-grown agent."],[24,"Coder workspace templates"],[607,"Coder workspace templates — what the two templates build and which\nvariable does what."],[812,"Coder workspace templates owns the templates, the create form and\nthe variables; Grok Build, Coder Agents, and the workspace terminal\nowns what runs inside the container once it is up."],[692,"Coder's optional AI Gateway proxy stays off - LiteLLM remains the model transport,\nwhich is why no AI-Gateway keys exist in `docker-compose.yml`."],[717,"Commands"],[736,"Compose supplies the provider: `HERMES_DASHBOARD_BASIC_AUTH_USERNAME`,\n`HERMES_DASHBOARD_BASIC_AUTH_PASSWORD` and `HERMES_DASHBOARD_BASIC_AUTH_SECRET`,\ninterpolated from `.env` with the same non-empty fallbacks `.env.sample`\ncarries (`admin` / `change-me-hermes` / `change-me-hermes-secret`). An empty\ninterpolation default is a boot error on `0.0.0.0`: the plugin skips\nregistration and the gateway refuses to bind."],[552,"Config files"],[821,"Config keys that gate all of this"],[1081,"Context7 or GitHub tools missing in Grok Build -> parked MCP block, or a handshake with nothing to authenticate"],[427,"Contributor environment"],[532,"Copy this shape; it is the convention every suite already uses (`use_stubs` prints nothing\nand shadows PATH for the current test only, and fails when a stub is missing):"],[573,"CPU, memory, CPU temperature and disk are host-wide through `/proc`. A network widget\nonly sees the container's own netns (`lo`/`eth0`) - `/sys/class/net` is namespaced, so\nthe host Wi-Fi NIC stays invisible even with `/sys` mounted. That tile reads `eth0`."],[605,"Create the first workspace. One repository per workspace is the default, and the template\npicks itself from the URL:"],[597,"Create the one file that holds real secrets, and lock it down before anything else reads\nit:"],[236,"Create the workspace it picks:"],[38,"Create-form fields"],[591,"Creating the first workspace from a git URL"],[33,"Credentials"],[477,"Credentials still arrive by the one supported path: Coder External Auth mints\n`GH_TOKEN`/`GITHUB_TOKEN`, and `--devcontainer` hands them to git through\n`gh auth setup-git`. There is no static token and no PAT in this repo's tooling."],[16,"Cut `feat/…`, `fix/…`, `refactor/…` (and `docs/…`, `test/…`, `chore/…`, `ci/…`) from the\ncurrent tip of `main`, one branch per change, and delete it the moment it merges. A branch\nthat outlives its change is a branch nobody rebases any more."],[393,"Daily commands"],[547,"Dashboard and desktops"],[728,"Dashboard on host