 the TLS handshake, checked from this box; the Hermes\nname is the same zone and the same proxy."],[490,"Do not copy the sentinel into another repository. An application repo's\n`.devcontainer/` is exactly what `new-workspace` is supposed to find, and the sentinel in\nfront of it silently downgrades that workspace to the plain template."],[216,"Docker creates the missing host directory itself (root-owned) and `startup.sh.tftpl`\nchowns it."],[41,"Docker-in-docker"],[1091,"Docker-in-docker"],[1118,"Docker-in-Docker, Terraform, and the host `coder` CLI"],[1002,"Dollar escaping differs across those two layers. A `templatefile()` `.tftpl` treats `$$`\nas an escaped `$` everywhere (`$name` or `$${name}`), and leaves `$((` arithmetic\nalone. An HCL heredoc in `main.tf` (`<<-EOT`) only escapes `$${name}` to `${name}`;\na lone `$` is already literal, so shell arithmetic is `$((...))` with one dollar.\n`$$((` is two dollars, and Coder runs `coder_script` bodies as `bash -c`, which\nexpands `$$` to the PID. Do not wrap `templatefile()` in `chomp()`."],[235,"Dry run (decision only, creates nothing):"],[448,"Each `KEY` there is also an `ARG` in `images/dev/Dockerfile`, and the `ARG` default\nmirrors the pin, so a bare `docker build` matches a scripted one."],[426,"Each CLI target also declares the repo files that script reads by path — `//:stack_data`\n(`docker-compose.yml`, both `templates/**` payload trees, `images/dev/**`,\n`.devcontainer/**`, `litellm/**`, `searxng/**`, `homepage/**`, `proxy/**`, the two `.env`\nsamples, `LICENSE`) and\n`//scripts:doc_sources` (every `scripts/**.sh`, so a sourced `scripts/lib/*.sh` resolves\ntoo). `proxy/certs/` is `.bazelignored` (bootstrap issues those on the host), so a\n`bazelisk run` of a stack runner or of `push-template` prefers `BUILD_WORKSPACE_DIRECTORY` — the real checkout —\nover the runfiles copy as the compose project directory, the live `.env`, and the template tree (runfiles\n`templates/**` are symlinks that Coder cannot follow after unpack). Without the committed payloads a\nsandboxed run would read a partial copy of the repo and fail for the wrong reason. A new\ntop-level payload directory has to be added to that `glob` by hand: `test-fast` and `lint`\nonly see repo files that travel in runfiles, so an unlisted directory is invisible to the\nharness rather than checked loosely."],[1123,"Each fence below is one copy-paste action. A heading quotes the error string where there\nis one, so start with `grep -n` on the text you saw."],[1042,"Each name is **one label under the zone**, and each service prefix joins it with a\n**hyphen**."],[705,"Each seeded file carries the `managed-by: evo-t1-coder-stack` marker - in\n`SKILL.md` directly under the `---` frontmatter, since the agent's skill parser\nrequires frontmatter on line 1 and silently drops anything else. Delete a file to\ntake it over; edit it and the stack leaves it alone. Either way the marker never\nreaches the model: the agent strips HTML comments from injected instruction text."],[377,"Each service name is **one label** under the zone and carries its prefix with a\n**HYPHEN**: a wildcard certificate covers exactly one label, so the dotted\ntwo-label form has no certificate at the public edge."],[249,"Each template creates one Docker container per workspace. Extra named volumes\n(`vscode-settings-<owner-id>` at `~/.shared/vscode`, and `grok-profile-<owner-id>`\nat `~/.grok` in shared mode) are chowned to the home owner at the start of\n`startup.sh.tftpl`, because Docker creates an empty named volume as `root:root`\n755 and the agent runs as `coder`."],[74,"Each template dir keeps its own independent copy of the `.tftpl` payloads\n(`startup.sh.tftpl`, `settings.json.tftpl`, `grok-config.toml.tftpl`). Change one twin,\nchange the other."],[648,"Each template's startup script probes `command -v grok` on every start and\nre-downloads from `https://x.ai/cli/install.sh` - bounded, with retries - only\nwhile `grok` is missing from PATH. That installer follows the `stable` pointer, not\nthis pin. It deliberately does **not** fetch on every boot: the bake-in under\n`/usr/local/bin` is the upgrade path, so shipping a new CLI means bumping the pin,\nrebuilding the image (`scripts/build-dev-image.sh`) and re-pushing the templates."],[922,"Each thinking alias carries the same hop of its own - `agent-low: [\"coder\"]`, and the\nsame for `agent-medium` and `agent-xhigh`. Groups are independent, so none of them\ninherits `agent`'s entry, and all four go down with exactly the same boxes."],[305,"Each workspace's agent then injects a `GIT_ASKPASS` helper that mints short-lived\nper-host tokens on demand, alongside a `GH_TOKEN`/`GITHUB_TOKEN` pair in the agent\nenvironment."],[938,"Edit `litellm/config.yaml`."],[839,"Editing an alias"],[83,"Editing the common copy changes both templates; the staged copy overwrites any\nsame-named file the template dir still carries."],[54,"Editor settings seed"],[1101,"Editor, credentials, the clone"],[1119,"Editor, credentials, the clone, UI logins, and the public names (`421`, Chat `4403`, Traefik)"],[52,"Editor, terminal, and the metadata tiles"],[568,"Either form rewrites `.env`, recreates the container and verifies the new value landed.\nThe script's job is keeping the secret out of shell history, `ps` and git, and leaving\n`.env` at mode 600."],[227,"Either way `folder` is the clone, so code-server and its terminal profiles land on the\nrepository, and the **Web Terminal** button `cd`s there too."],[1150,"Either way keep `SPARK_n_API_KEY` non-empty: `SPARK_1_API_KEY`, `SPARK_2_API_KEY`,\n`SPARK_3_API_KEY`. An empty key fails every request inside the proxy before it ever\nreaches the box."],[258,"Ensures the **Grok Build CLI** is on PATH. The golden image ships it, so the\n`https://x.ai/cli/install.sh` download runs only where `grok` is missing from PATH -\nthe `ubuntu:24.04` image option, or a home volume that never received the CLI."],[376,"Entries are DNS names, not URLs: no scheme, no port, no path. The entry with no\nprefix is the dashboard."],[22,"Environments are where future protection rules and secrets go, per environment:\n`development`, `staging`, `production`. `production` stays restricted to `main` — or to\ntags — with required reviewers. See the header comment in `.github/workflows/ci.yml`."],[1035,"Every `location` adds `X-Evo-Proxy` with the upstream name, and `always` is what\nmakes it survive a 502. Read it beside `X-Coder-Request-Id`, which Coder's own proxy\nsets on an answered request: neither header means the request stopped at Traefik or\nCloudflare, and `421` means the Host header matched no server block here."],[988,"Every `scripts/**/*.sh` file starts with a `# ## ` header that names the file and says whether it is an entry point or a sourced library."],[861,"Every alias is a stable name. A workspace setting never has to change when a backend\nmoves behind one."],[61,"Every create-form field and template variable, with its default"],[349,"Every flag goes **after** the subcommand, so `update-configs --dry-run env` is a\nusage error and prints the usage rather than guessing."],[989,"Every function carries this block immediately above the definition:"],[991,"Every function under `scripts/` is named by an asserting test under `tests/`: one suite per\nmodule, plus one test per entry-level function that drives the whole script (`tests/bats/\nentry-fns.bats` is where those live). `tests/shell_inventory.sh` fails when a name is\nmissing, and `tests/doc_coverage.sh` when a `# @function` block is missing or incomplete.\nTests are hermetic: docker, ssh, curl, git and the other external tools resolve through\n`tests/bats/tool_stubs`."],[514,"Every suite under `tests/` is hermetic Bats: it runs against stubs and a throwaway tree,\nnever against a daemon, a network, or the operator's real `.env`."],[659,"Every workspace gets its own `/home/coder` volume, and `~/.grok` is a **second,\nnested** mount inside it: a Docker volume named `grok-profile-<owner-id>`,\nreferenced by name rather than declared as a Terraform resource, which every\nworkspace of that owner mounts read-write at the same path **while that workspace is\nin `shared` mode**."],[108,"Everything Coder-facing runs **inside the coder container**, against\n`http://127.0.0.1:3000`."],[411,"Everything else is a Bazel target, including every `scripts/*.sh`. CI repeats the gate from\na clean runner inside the same golden image: `.github/workflows/ci.yml` builds\n`images/dev` with buildx and the Actions layer cache and docker-runs the two suites below in\nit, so the bazel job does not install the pins onto the runner at all — the image already\ncarries them. The persistent cache on that path is the buildx GHA layer cache, so a pull\nrequest that leaves `images/dev/**` alone replays the image layers."],[993,"Everything else is a Bazel target:"],[962,"Everything else is a target those two feed:"],[776,"evo-t1-coder-stack"],[1247,"Existing workspaces pick up the buttons after `bazelisk run //scripts:push-template`\nand a workspace update to the new template version."],[546,"Exit `5` with one `unresolvable repo root` line beats guessing a cwd and half-running a\nfleet check against a copy of the repo."],[634,"Explaining why one workspace's `~/.grok` disagrees with another's"],[1025,"Exposing the stack without breaking the LAN routes anyone at home uses"],[999,"External tools are probed with `command -v` and reported as \"not on PATH\", not assumed.\n`require_tool` skips locally and fails under `CI=true`."],[834,"Fallback: `agent` to `coder`"],[741,"Fallbacks, in the order worth trying them:"],[974,"File header"],[303,"Fill every `CODER_EXTERNAL_AUTH_0_*` key or omit them all. A defined-but-empty key\ncrash-loops the server, which is why these keys live in `coder.env` and not in `.env`."],[585,"First boot"],[583,"First boot on a GMKtec EVO-T1, top to bottom — bootstrap the host, bring the stable stack up, register Coder, push the templates, open a workspace."],[1153,"First run this to see the plan, then run it again without the flag to apply it:"],[1210,"Fix with the `docker pull` above, or turn DinD off for that workspace."],[1147,"Fix, one of these:"],[1232,"Fix: `coder_app` resources are not gated on `start_count` (scripts, metadata\nand the container still are). Push the templates; new creates stop showing the\nwarning. Existing workspaces pick it up on the next update to the new template\nversion."],[1213,"Fix: `docker-compose.yml` sets `dns: [1.1.1.1, 8.8.8.8]` on the `coder`\nservice (embedded DNS still answers `db` and other compose names). Both\ntemplates pin the same resolvers on the workspace and DinD containers so\na later `git clone` of `github.com` does not hit the same SERVFAIL. Recreate\n`coder` so the new upstreams apply, then push:"],[1126,"Fix: `homepage/**` and `proxy/*.conf` belong in `//:stack_data`, and the stack\nrunners prefer `BUILD_WORKSPACE_DIRECTORY` (the real checkout) so relative\nmounts and bootstrap-issued `proxy/certs/` resolve there. Re-run from the stack\nhost:"],[1220,"Fix: `push-template` now prefers `BUILD_WORKSPACE_DIRECTORY` (the live\ncheckout) and stages with `tar -h` so the archive holds regular files. Pull\nthis commit onto the stack host and re-run:"],[1186,"Fix: check that version in `images/dev/tool-versions.env` against the upstream\nrelease, then rebuild the image."],[1260,"Fix: compose interpolation defaults now match `.env.sample`\n(`change-me-hermes` / `change-me-hermes-secret`). Recreate the service:"],[1226,"Fix: point the CLI at the container's loopback listener, `http://127.0.0.1:3000`,\nwhich nothing can gate. See \"Coder workspace templates\" in README.md."],[1130,"Fix: recover from a shell, then re-run. `--repair` uses sudo when chmod is not\nenough:"],[1234,"Fix: the increment is `waited=$((waited + 1))` (one dollar). Push the templates and\nrestart so the editor script relaunches."],[1236,"Fix: the inlined fork starts code-server with `--ignore-last-opened` and the\nclone folder as a positional argument (`/home/coder/workspace/<repo>` on the\n`workspace` template). Push the templates and restart so the editor process\nrelaunches."],[1217,"Fix: the SVG is a compact ribbon whose data URL fits the column, and\n`push-template` rejects a too-large copy locally before talking to the server.\nPull this commit onto the stack host and re-run:"],[1201,"Fix: the template chowns that volume (and the shared `~/.grok` profile volume)\nto the home owner before the seed, and skips `jq`/`python` when the write\nfails. Push the templates and restart the workspace; there is nothing to delete."],[562,"Fixing a card that reports down when the service itself is up"],[320,"Flags"],[1141,"Flags are accepted before or after `logs`; `--project-name` and `--tail` move either\nway. Only `logs` takes trailing service names, and here that trailing word is the\nservice to read."],[237,"Force the `workspace` template:"],[241,"Found means `devcontainer`; not found means `workspace`. A probe that fails **entirely**\nis also a `workspace` answer, with a warning."],[695,"Four files seed into every new workspace, on first boot and only while the file is\nabsent:"],[48,"From a git URL: `bazelisk run //scripts:new-workspace`"],[479,"From a machine that is **not** inside the container, ask the image to run them instead of\ninstalling the toolchain onto that machine:"],[975,"Functions"],[783,"Getting oriented in one screen before opening a terminal"],[582,"Getting started"],[1014,"Getting the naming right"],[403,"Getting the same Bazel, Bats, shellcheck and Terraform that CI uses without installing\nany of them"],[960,"Getting to the right runbook in one click instead of searching the README"],[1107,"gh_token_refresh says gh would not store the minted token"],[432,"GitHub auth in the container"],[440,"GitHub auth inside the container, and why `github-auth check` runs SELF there"],[1008,"GitHub auth is Coder External Auth, id `github`