icial Web\nDashboard with a Chat tab that carries approval prompts, so the assistant can plan a\nchange, show the plan, and wait for you to approve it before it touches anything."],[1041,"Hermes is the same additive hop as the other four. Traefik forwards\n`http://<this-box-lan-ip>:8080` with the original Host, and the router sends that\nHost to `http://hermes:9119`. The LAN URL `http://<STACK_LAN_HOST>:9119` stays.\nHTTP basic auth on the dashboard stays too; Authelia is the extra public gate.\nSee hermes.md."],[734,"Hermes since the June 2026 hardening refuses a non-loopback bind without a\n`DashboardAuthProvider`. Binding `0.0.0.0` with no provider is a boot error, not a\nwarning."],[738,"Hermes talks to the LiteLLM proxy the stack already runs: base URL\n`http://litellm:4000/v1`, model alias **`agent`**. That is the tool-capable Spark lane,\nwhich is what an agent loop needs, and it stays the default."],[497,"Hermetic Bats: how a suite is discovered, what the stub PATH gives you, and the two inventory gates a new function has to satisfy."],[549,"Homepage dashboard"],[1214,"Host `git pull` still needs a public resolver beside MagicDNS when the host\nitself is MagicDNS-only (heading above; `setup-host --repair` on Linux).\nExisting workspaces pick up the container DNS on the next start after this\ntemplate version is active."],[554,"Host stats, and the docker socket"],[60,"How `push-template.sh` ships the source, and the same push by hand"],[29,"How `push-template` works"],[1076,"How do I know the IPEX-LLM server came up? -> look for `runners=[ipex_llm]`"],[803,"How the pieces fit"],[782,"How the sidebar tabs divide the subjects"],[8,"How to cut, name and delete a short-lived work branch"],[718,"How to reach the dashboard, on the LAN and on the public name"],[767,"HTTP basic auth stays, including on the public URL. Authelia is the gate in front of\nthat name only. LAN `:9119` and a matching Host on `:8080` bypass Authelia, so the\nbasic-auth provider is load-bearing. It is a provider, not a toggle."],[924,"If a concurrency cap is ever reintroduced, its pairing is `fallbacks` plus\n`context_window_fallbacks`. Both, not one."],[1245,"If that page says \"You must install the GitHub App to clone private repositories\"\nand lists no accounts, the device-flow login already succeeded. Click **Install\nGitHub App** on the workspace (or open\ngithub.com/apps/coder/installations/new),\ngrant the private repos, then restart. Coder's injected provider omits\n`AppInstallURL`, so the warning on `/external-auth/github` is unlinked plaintext."],[1166,"If the SearXNG lane stays down, native search is already on. Park the failing\nserver with `search_mcp = false` on the next template push (`SEARCH_MCP=false` in\n`.env` applies it to every new workspace). To park native search instead, set\n`disable_web_search = true` in the workspace's `~/.grok/config.toml` and start a\nnew session."],[1279,"If the UI is unreachable, check that `CODER_ACCESS_URL` matches the address you are\nbrowsing from: the LAN IP by default, or the public coder name in public mode."],[683,"If you know a real experiment you want (`chat-advisor`, `chat-virtual-desktop`,\n...), list it in `.env` and restart the coder service. Empty means no experiments\non."],[250,"Image from `images/dev/Dockerfile` (overridable with the `image` variable) carrying:\nNode 22 + 24, Python 3.12 + 3.11, Go 1.24, Bazelisk/buildifier,\nTerraform/tflint/terragrunt, protoc and its Go plugins, kubectl/helm/kubeconform,\nshfmt/shellcheck/bats/ruff/mypy/prettier, the Coder CLI, and the pinned Grok Build CLI\nat `/usr/local/bin/grok`."],[1085,"Image missing tools, or the build aborts mid-layer -> `curl: (22)`"],[664,"In `shared` mode: `config.toml`, `skills/`, `memory-v2/`, `sessions/`, `notes/` (the\ncanonical copy of each repository's private scratch `notes.md`), and a CLI you\ninstalled yourself under `~/.grok/bin`."],[913,"In `shared` profile mode that is one file per user, re-rendered by the last-booted\nworkspace, which then shares that key across that user's workspaces."],[977,"Ingress"],[982,"Ingress rules: what runs from a shell and what is a Bazel target"],[217,"Inside a built dev container the same folder appears under `/workspaces/<repo-name>`,\nthe devcontainer CLI's default mount target and where the dev-container editor opens."],[357,"Inside a running container the same seven targets are `refresh-configs`'s job\ntoo: same reseed set, same marker rule, `--json` for a machine-readable\nanswer, and `--litellm-url <url>` for a stack environment that publishes\nLiteLLM on a port other than 4000 (the reseeded `settings.json` then still\nnames that stack's own model transport). grok-build-and-agents.md covers the profile\nvolume and what seeds on first boot."],[859,"Inside a workspace the key travels as the `LITELLM_API_KEY` environment variable, which\n`~/.grok/config.toml` references by `env_key`, so no key byte lands in a file."],[527,"Inside the contributor dev container (devcontainer.md) the commands\nabove are exactly what CI runs."],[50,"Inside the workspace container"],[1249,"Inside the workspace, run `GH_TOKEN= GITHUB_TOKEN= gh auth status`. Then click\n**GitHub reauth**, finish device-code login, install the Coder GitHub App if the\nreauth page says to, and restart."],[678,"Installing Cline, Roo, the Red Hat YAML extension and Material Icon Theme is a\nmanual step in the Extensions panel (Open VSX by default). If an extension build\nnames its settings differently, set the OpenAI-compatible endpoint and key in its\nUI."],[314,"Installing one REPLACES the credential that workspace was presenting. While an\naccount *is* connected the store holds a minted pair and the next `gh_token_refresh`\nrun (start, then every 6 hours) rewrites it, so the PAT is a stand-in, not a second\npermanent credential: rotate or remove it in GitHub -> Settings -> Applications when\nthe work ends. `gh auth logout`, or a rebuild, clears the store either way."],[257,"Installs `tmux` if it is missing, then seeds `~/.tmux.conf` (only while that file is\nabsent or still carries the `managed-by: evo-t1-coder-stack` marker)."],[842,"IPEX-LLM over vanilla Ollama"],[889,"It behaves that way on both `/api/chat` and `/v1/chat/completions`."],[231,"It carries its own copies of `startup.sh.tftpl`, `settings.json.tftpl` and\n`grok-config.toml.tftpl`, so the tmux-default terminal and LiteLLM wiring above apply\nto it too."],[95,"It confirms an **active** version."],[901,"It decides only for unpinned traffic: the affinity pin below resolves first, and\n`least-busy` runs when nothing is pinned, when the pinned deployment is unhealthy or in\ncooldown, and for any request with no session id."],[355,"It does not touch `~/.grok/config.toml`. That file is rendered *inside* the\nworkspace, and `~/.grok` is one profile volume per owner, so a copy from the\nhost would move the model list, the session-affinity key and the editor keys\nof every workspace sharing the profile. A **start/restart** re-renders it from\nthis checkout, which is the only way a per-workspace value gets in, and the\npass says so after it reseeds."],[245,"It either runs the command (`--no-wait`; watch with `coder ls` / `coder logs <name>`)\nor, with no usable `coder` login, prints the same command to run by hand and exits 0."],[671,"It is **not** a model transport, so `web_search = \"agent\"` and\n`supports_backend_search = false` stay as they are and the agent's own `web_search`\ntool still digests through the `agent` alias. Native search is the default:\n`disable_web_search = false` keeps the `web_search` tool in the session (it has no\nhosted backend on this box - LiteLLM answers \"tools of type 'web_search' are not\nsupported\" - so the client-side scrape path is what runs). The `searxng` MCP stdio\nserver is the fallback: both templates render that block gated on `search_mcp`,\nwhich defaults to true. To park native search, set `disable_web_search` to true\nand start a new session. Measure the self-hosted lane with:"],[107,"It is also the manual path after you register an account, and the retry path for one\ntemplate."],[622,"It is always on"],[239,"It looks for a dev container in `.devcontainer/`, `.github/devcontainers/`, or a\n`devcontainer.json`/`devcontainer.yml` anywhere in the tree."],[244,"It names no `--stop-after`, so a script-made workspace gets no autostop deadline."],[354,"It never drops a key your env file still sets; retired keys are commented out\nin place."],[248,"It never mints, reads, or stores a token - unlike `push-template.sh`, which mints its\nown because a template push has no other credential path. With `CODER_SESSION_TOKEN`\nset but `CODER_URL` unset it refuses to guess, and an empty token is a *not yet* state\nrather than an error."],[353,"It never prints an env value that looks like a credential."],[472,"It never writes a secret, never writes a GitHub token or a PAT, and never installs the\nGrok CLI — the golden image already carries `/usr/local/bin/grok`. Exit `5` means no\nproven checkout was found (it wants `docker-compose.yml` where it is looking), which is the\nsame repo-root probe every other script in the repo makes."],[97,"It re-pins **Autostop** to *Disabled*."],[96,"It re-sends the template's own description."],[92,"It rejects a `coder_workspace_preset` description over Coder's 128-**byte** ceiling."],[93,"It rejects a `vscode-alt.svg` whose inlined data URL would exceed Coder's\n256-character `workspace_apps.icon` column."],[89,"It resolves the repo root from `BUILD_WORKSPACE_DIRECTORY` (the real checkout\n`bazelisk run` names) ahead of the runfiles copy, so `.env` and the template\nfiles are regular files rather than execroot symlinks."],[90,"It resolves the running stack on the Docker **daemon** by container label, never\nthrough a cwd-resolved compose project."],[113,"It runs the image's own `coder` binary, so client and server are the same build."],[238,"It shallow-clones (`--depth 1 --no-checkout --single-branch`) into a temporary\ndirectory, from the host, and lists the tracked files."],[1154,"It skips while the coder or db container is down, or nobody has registered yet, and\nre-running it repairs a provider that drifted."],[935,"It spread 12/10/8 across the three deployments and returned 30x 200."],[94,"It streams the source as a tar on stdin, with symlinks dereferenced into regular\nfiles. Coder's provisioner unpacks that archive into an empty workdir and does\nnot follow host paths, so a stored runfiles symlink plans as \"No configuration\nfiles\"."],[243,"It then assembles `coder create` with the template's parameters: `repo_url=<url>`\nalways, `use_devcontainer=false` whenever `devcontainer` was chosen but no dev\ncontainer was found (forced with `--devcontainer` onto a repo that has none, or a probe\nthat could not check the repo - the cases where leaving the toggle at its default would\nbuild nothing anyway), `dind=true` on `--dind`, and `additional_repos=<list>` whenever\n`--additional-repos` named at least one extra URL."],[923,"It used to be a chain, `agent -> agent-fast -> coder`. `agent-fast` was a second alias\nfor the same model on a second box with a lower output ceiling; one group of three equal\ndeployments already covers every reachable box, so the chain collapsed to one acyclic\nhop."],[900,"Its counters are per deployment and expire after a hardcoded 3600 s; there is no\n`routing_strategy_args` block to set, and `ttl` there would be a paste from newer docs."],[111,"Its first unauthenticated call (the first-user check) gets the HTML sign-in page back,\nand the CLI reports that as `unexpected non-JSON response \"text/html; charset=utf-8\"`."],[1146,"Its host list comes from the `SPARK*_URL` keys in `.env` (`SPARKn_OLLAMA_URL` and\n`SPARKn_OPENAI_URL`), which is why the default run needs no arguments. Export\n`SPARK_HOSTS=\"host1 host2 ...\"` in the process environment only to check a fleet that\n`.env` does not name. A host that does not answer is a skip, not a failure."],[927,"Its per-box widgets go to error state while `agent` still answers, because `agent`\nanswers from the Arc while every Spark is down."],[118,"Its scope has to be `coder:all` with `allow_list` `{*:*}`: a narrowed token fails the\nCLI's opening organization lookups, so least privilege is not available on v2.36."],[580,"Kasm is a privileged Docker-in-Docker container and the only **always-on** privileged\nservice in this stack - the other privileged container is the opt-in workspace DinD\nsidecar. Keep Kasm LAN-only unless you have decided who may reach the public name\n(see SECURITY.md)."],[1032,"Kasm is the only hop that speaks TLS to its origin. `proxy_ssl_verify` is off there\nbecause the certificate is the one Kasm's installer generates and reissues. Hermes,\nlike Homepage, Coder and LiteLLM, is plain HTTP at the origin (`http://hermes:9119`)."],[1068,"Kasm stores its connection endpoints in its own setup database (first-boot wizard or\nadmin UI), so the endpoint has to change there too or streams keep dialing the LAN\naddress."],[1113,"Kasm wizard gone after install -> expected"],[556,"Kasm Workspaces"],[560,"Kasm's wizard-and-UI port pair, and what resetting it destroys"],[292,"Keep it that way unless a workspace genuinely needs two trees open at once."],[190,"Keep the other licensed flags out of the CE stack too. `--failure-ttl` (Failure\ncleanup), `--dormancy-threshold` and `--dormancy-auto-deletion` are all marked \"This\nlicensed feature's default is 0h (off)\" in `templates edit --help` on v2.36.6, and\n`--allow-user-autostart` works the same way. Older notes also list `--inactivityTTL`\namong the rejected names; v2.36.6 has no flag of that name, and `--default-ttl` and\n`--activity-bump` are the closest."],[316,"Keeping a checkout's config current"],[667,"Keyed by **owner id**, never host-wide and never cross-user: another user's\nworkspace mounts a differently named volume, and a stop or start of a *different\nuser's* workspace never sees the volume at all."],[35,"Knobs and skips"],[1121,"Knowing the cost of a fix before running it, including what it destroys"],[12,"Knowing which green check actually gates a merge into `main`"],[810,"Knowing which page owns a concept when two of them seem to"],[593,"Knowing which step to re-run when a later one says a prerequisite is missing"],[498,"Layout"],[801,"Learn the stack"],[757,"Leave the mode on `manual`. `off` is `--yolo`: every mutating command executes on the\nhost with no card."],[388,"Leaving all three `SPARKn_OPENAI_URL` keys empty keeps `agent` defined but\nunusable: LiteLLM then falls back to `coder`, the Arc alias. That fallback is what\nthe \"Agent backend\" card exists to catch - Grok Build, Cline and Roo need\nstructured tool calls, which the Arc IPEX-LLM Ollama returns as plain text for the\nQwen2.5-Coder weights. litellm-routing.md owns the alias\ntable, the picker, the pin, and the measured tool-call limitation (including which\naliases do emit real calls)."],[816,"LiteLLM model routing"],[608,"LiteLLM model routing — why the answer you got came from the box it\ncame from."],[551,"Login"],[555,"Look"],[1143,"Look at the dashboard's **Agent backend** card first: its per-box widgets go to error\nstate while `agent` still answers."],[112,"Loopback inside the container cannot be gated, so the push cannot fail that way."],[581,"Losing the wizard after install is expected: use `:4443`. Resetting Kasm means\nremoving the `kasm-data` volume, which destroys all Kasm config."],[3,"main"],[512,"Making a new function satisfy `//tests:shell_inventory` without guessing"],[986,"Matching the house style instead of inventing a local one"],[887,"Measured against this box's IPEX-LLM Ollama, whose bundled `ollama` is 0.9.3."],[933,"Measured on a harness boot of this config against the live Spark boxes, before\n`session_affinity` existed."],[270,"Memory (90 percent) and disk (85 percent, `/home/coder`) usage gauges, six resource\nmetadata tiles sampled every 30s - four `coder stat` calls (`cpu --host`,\n`mem --host`, `disk --path /home/coder`, `cpu --host`) and two awk one-liners for swap\nand load average."],[1075,"Model lane: Spark, LiteLLM, the agent backends"],[623,"Model wiring"],[712,"Models"],[843,"MoE over dense"],[713,"Mounts and \"be the host\""],[851,"Moving a workload between the Arc iGPU and a Spark box without touching a workspace"],[523,"Name it in exactly one suite. A chain test that happens to mention the name also satisfies\nthe inventory, but the owning suite is the one that asserts its behaviour."],[18,"Name the branch after the change, not the author, and keep the commit subject imperative\nwith one of `feat:`, `fix:`, `docs:`, `test:`, `chore:`, `ci:`, `refactor:`."],[215,"Named volumes cannot substitute: a volume is a daemon-local object and does not cross\nto the sidecar's daemon."],[980,"Names and flags"],[984,"Names, flags, and the style guide shell follows"],[11,"Naming a branch and a commit so CI and `git log` read the way the rest of the repo does"],[481,"Native `bazelisk test` on macOS is a convenience, not a merge path. The suites run there,\nbut the BSD userland differs from the GNU one the image ships (`sed`, `date`, `find`,\n`sort`), so a green Darwin run is not the run that gates the merge and a red one is not\nproof of a defect. The container, or `test-in-image`, is the answer\ntest-with-bazel.md and ../branching.md gate on."],[1177,"Neither header, and a `Server: cloudflare` with a `cf-ray` instead: Traefik or\nCloudflare answered, and there is nothing on this box to read."],[941,"Neither stack runner has a `restart` subcommand (`up`, `down`, `status`, `logs`, `reset`\nare the whole set), so the proxy restart stays a direct compose call. Stable stack:"],[643,"Neither template installs code-server through the Registry. Each `main.tf` carries\nan inlined fork (`coder_script.code_server` + `coder_app.code_server`), because the\nupstream module hardcodes `/icon/code.svg` and has no icon input. `workspace`\ninstalls code-server only when it is missing from `/home/coder/.local/share/code-server`\nand starts it with `--auth none --port 13337 --app-name \"VS Code Web\"\n--ignore-last-opened <folder>`, passing no settings payload. `devcontainer` has no\npersistent prefix to reuse, so it installs fresh under `/tmp/code-server` on every\nstart."],[273,"Neither template installs code-server through the Registry. Each `main.tf` carries an\ninlined fork (`coder_script.code_server` + `coder_app.code_server`) because that\nupstream module hardcodes `/icon/code.svg` and has no icon input. The script body\nlives in a sibling `code-server.sh.tftpl` and is rendered with `templatefile()`\n(workspace: `{ editor_folder = local.editor_folder }`; devcontainer: that plus\n`settings_b64`). Do not wrap that `templatefile()` in `chomp()`."],[98,"No `.terraform.lock.hcl` is committed under `templates/`. Each `main.tf` pins\n`coder/coder` `~> 2.18` and `kreuzwerker/docker` `~> 4.6` in `required_providers`; Coder\npushes with a warning when no lockfile sits beside them. `coder_devcontainer` needs a\nserver `>= 2.21`, which this stack runs (v2.36.6)."],[228,"No `config_path` is set, so the CLI discovers the file the way VS Code does, and a repo\nusing the other legal locations behaves the same."],[995,"No `eval`. Prefer `\"${var}\"`, `[[ ]]`, and `$(...)`."],[483,"No Actions `container:` key is involved. The job runs on a plain runner and reaches the\ntoolchain through `docker run --user \"$(id -u):$(id -g)\"` with `HOME=/tmp` and\n`USER=$(id -un)`, so what gates the merge is an image tag, the bind-mounted checkout\nstays writable, permission tests see a non-root identity, and Bazel can name a uid the\nimage passwd file does not list."],[104,"No arguments pushes every template in `TEMPLATES_DEFAULT` order."],[771,"No GitHub PAT in Hermes. GitHub auth in this stack is Coder External Auth only, and a\ntoken here would sit on a container that can both write to the checkout and drive the\nhost daemon. See SECURITY.md."],[114,"No host `coder` CLI and no `coder login` are involved, and a stale host-side session\ncannot aim the push at some other deployment."],[179,"Notes on the two dropdowns that take a custom value:"],[123,"Nothing else about GitHub travels in a `--var`."],[1033,"Nothing in this path replaces the LAN routes: `https://<lan-ip>/` still serves the\ndashboard on the self-signed cert, `https://<lan-ip>:3001` still serves Coder's\nown TLS listener, and `http://<STACK_LAN_HOST>:9119` still serves Hermes."],[1051,"Nothing in this repo configures Traefik. This is the file the other box needs: drop it\nin the directory that box's `providers.file.directory` watches and Traefik picks it up\nwithout a restart. The shape below is the one Traefik v2 and v3 both read; the\nentryPoint name, the certificate and the middleware name have to match what that box\nalready defines, so treat those three as the values to align, not as new requirements."],[15,"Nothing is committed straight to `main`. Integration into `main` is by pull request, and a\nPR is only mergeable once CI is green:\n`bazelisk test //:test-fast` and `bazelisk test //:lint --test_tag_filters=manual`, both\nexecuted inside the golden image (`images/dev/Dockerfile`) that CI builds with buildx and\ndocker-runs — the toolchain comes from that image, not from anything installed onto the\nrunner. Locally, run them the same way: inside the contributor container\n(contribute/devcontainer.md) or with\n`bazelisk run //scripts:test-in-image --`. `bash scripts/setup-host.sh` is the bootstrap\nfor the stack host, where the suites have to run on the host itself;\n`bazelisk run //:validate` runs both of the checks plus\n`docker compose config -q` and the `.env.sample`/`.env.example` comparison — that is the\npre-PR gate."],[203,"Nothing is published to the host, and 2375 is reachable only from that workspace's own\nnetwork - which is also why the network is not `internal`. An internal network gets no\ngateway route or NAT, so `host.docker.internal` would resolve and never answer, and the\nagent would strand. See SECURITY.md."],[308,"Nothing long-lived lives in any file, env or template: the rendered `config.toml`\nnames `GH_TOKEN` and nothing else, and the pair stops at the workspace container's edge\n(a dev container built on the sidecar is not handed either key)."],[745,"Nous Portal is an optional upstream, not a default, and this page does not document it.\nNothing here needs an account."],[799,"Ollama is reachable only from inside the compose network: LiteLLM is the gateway, and it\nis the thing that carries the master key."],[1240,"On `devcontainer`:"],[528,"On a host that is not that container, `//scripts:test-in-image` docker-runs\n`evo-t1-dev:latest` as this process's uid:gid, with `HOME=/tmp` and `USER` set so\nBazel can name that uid, and runs them there."],[950,"On a memory-rich but bandwidth- and latency-constrained iGPU that is the sweet spot,\nbecause an equivalent dense model would move every parameter per token and run much\nslower at the same footprint."],[350,"On a TTY the env pass asks by default (`-i`/`--interactive` is then a no-op;\n`--non-interactive` turns it off). For every key that is new this pull or still\n`change-me…`/`NOTSET`/`YOUR_LAN_IP` it prints the explanation the twin carries\nabove that key and prompts for a value. Enter keeps a reusable value already\nset in a sibling env file, or the example default. A key whose\nname carries `KEY`, `SECRET`, `TOKEN` or `PASSWORD` is echoed nowhere - the\nreport says `set` or `empty` and the prompt does not echo what you type - so a\nscreenful of this output is safe to paste into an issue. With no terminal to\nprompt through the pass warns and leaves those keys alone, which is why\n`--dry-run` / `--non-interactive` is the shape that belongs in a script or CI."],[1133,"On Linux, `bash scripts/setup-host.sh --repair` writes\n`/etc/systemd/resolved.conf.d/evo-t1-public-dns.conf` (`DNS=1.1.1.1 8.8.8.8`),\nruns `sudo tailscale set --accept-dns=false`, and keeps MagicDNS for `ts.net`\nvia `resolvectl` split-DNS. `--check` still writes nothing."],[1254,"On the host it enumerates the labeled workspace containers with docker and probes\neach (a named container checks just that one). Inside a workspace the docker CLI\nreaches only that workspace's DinD sidecar, so the same command runs SELF mode\nwith no docker: one probe of this environment's own credential chain, printed as\none `self:` line per credential. Pass only the repo URL there; a named container is\nrefused and pointed at the host shell. The repo URL may be the clone URL or the\nbrowser URL, with or without a trailing slash and `.git`; a path below `owner/repo`\nis refused rather than probed, because it names no repository. Full usage:\n`bazelisk run //scripts:github-auth -- --help`."],[1244,"On the workspace page, click **GitHub reauth**. Coder opens `/external-auth/<id>`\n(device flow for the injected App, OAuth for a custom app in `coder.env`). If the\npage says you are already authenticated, click **Reauthenticate**."],[586,"Once Coder answers"],[521,"one asserting test in the **one** suite for its module — a `scripts/lib/<mod>.sh` helper\nbelongs to `tests/bats/<mod>.bats`, and a helper that only an entry CLI defines belongs to\n`tests/bats/entry-fns.bats`, which loads single functions with `load_shell_function`;"],[777,"One compose stack that turns a GMKtec EVO-T1 into a self-hosted dev-workspace server — Coder, LiteLLM, IPEX-LLM Ollama, Kasm, Homepage and Hermes."],[309,"One connection covers every workspace, and `gh auth status` inside a workspace is how\nyou check it landed."],[905,"One conversation from one client sticks to the box that answered its first turn, for as\nlong as that box stays healthy."],[898,"One endpoint per box, one box per endpoint. Never point two deployments, or two\naliases, at the same physical machine: the proxy counts deployments, not machines."],[818,"One front door"],[828,"One group, three deployments"],[212,"One host bind, `/srv/coder-devcontainers/<workspace-id>`, mounted at that **identical**\npath in both containers."],[219,"One host-side path for all three would open the editor on a folder that exists nowhere\nthe editor runs, and VS Code answers that with\n`Workspace does not exist. Please select another workspace to open.`"],[446,"One image — `images/dev/Dockerfile`, built as `evo-t1-dev:latest` — is the contributor and\ntest runtime on macOS, on Linux, and on GitHub. The same Dockerfile serves the Coder\nworkspaces the stack provisions, the contributor dev container on a laptop, and the\ncontainer CI docker-runs its checks inside. Every version in it comes from\n`images/dev/tool-versions.env`; ../coder-templates.md covers the\nworkspace side, and CONTRIBUTING.md\nis the checklist the PR follows."],[996,"One language per file where reasonable. A bash, python, or awk program that lives\ninside another file is its own tested file, imported with `source`, `cat` + `sh -c`\n/ `ssh`, `python3 file.py`, `awk -f`, or Terraform `file()` / `templatefile()`. Keep\n1–3 line awk, usage heredocs, Dockerfiles, YAML data, docs fences, and\n`python3 -m webbrowser`. Remote probes are POSIX and self-contained under\n`scripts/lib/probes/`; the host `cat`s them and tests run the file with `sh`."],[983,"One language per file, the shared log contract, and the payload copies the templates share"],[813,"One OpenAI-compatible door, several backends behind it: the Arc 140T through IPEX-LLM, and\noptional Spark boxes. Which one answers is a routing decision made in\nlitellm-routing.md, not in the client — and that page also states the\none thing the local model cannot do."],[194,"One privileged `docker:29.8.1-dind` sidecar on a bridge network private to that\nworkspace (`coder-<wsid>-dind`, network alias `dind`)."],[290,"One repository per workspace is the default, and that is what `repo_url` and the\n**Git repository** field mean: one URL, cloned into one folder."],[669,"One shared profile is one `config.toml` for every workspace that owner owns, and\nthe last boot to re-render it wins - for the default model, the affinity key and\nthe config extras alike."],[630,"One shared profile volume per user, and what last-booted rewrites"],[209,"One workspace container from the golden image: launcher and clone target only. It still\nhas to be the golden image, because that is what ships the Docker client the\ndevcontainer flow talks through. The editor's real environment is whatever the repo\nbuilds, so `image` decides nothing about the toolchain inside it."],[1191,"One-off fix, from the stack host:"],[200,"Only the literal string `\"true\"` enables it; anything else reads as off."],[430,"Open it on a laptop"],[406,"Open the checkout in the contributor dev container (`.devcontainer/devcontainer.json`\nbuilds it) and run the commands below unchanged."],[438,"Opening the repo as a contributor container in VS Code or a compatible editor"],[953,"Operate the box"],[997,"Operator CLIs source `scripts/lib/common.sh` and do not redefine `log` / `die` /\n`skip`. Grouping: `section` prints `== name ==`, `phase` prints `-> text`, `ok`\nprints `ok: text`, `summary` prints `summary: N ok, W warnings, F failed` plus\n`  failed: …` and optional `next: cmd`. `JSON_MODE` set sends prose to stderr.\nCLIs without `--json` unset `JSON_MODE` after source. Keep prefixes `warning:` /\n`note:` / `error:`."],[192,"Opt-in in `workspace` (the **Docker-in-docker** Yes/No question, preset *AI workspace +\nDinD*, template variable `dind`). With the toggle off, `docker` in that workspace fails\nthe normal way rather than against a daemon that does not exist."],[1145,"Or check the whole fleet at once, from the checkout. `spark-verify.sh` takes `--json`\nand `--no-tests`; `--no-tests` skips the recipe's own probes (a 195k-token needle plus\na 1/2/4/5-client sweep, minutes per box) and leaves the quick read-only check:"],[1256,"Or install a write-capable PAT into one workspace's gh auth store, on stdin:"],[1149,"Or repoint `SPARK1_OPENAI_URL`, `SPARK2_OPENAI_URL` and `SPARK3_OPENAI_URL` in `.env`\nat a tool-capable OpenAI-compatible endpoint, then restart the proxy so it re-reads\nthem. The stack runners have no `restart` subcommand, so this one stays a direct\ncompose call:"],[407,"Or, from a machine that is not in that container, `bazelisk run //scripts:test-in-image --`\ndocker-runs `evo-t1-dev:latest` and runs the gate inside it."],[476,"Pass only the repository URL. A named container argument is refused with a pointer to the\nhost shell, because that container lives on a daemon this environment cannot enumerate."],[91,"Per template it checks `main.tf` exists (otherwise \"run this from the repo root\") and\nnotes a missing `.terraform.lock.hcl`."],[1193,"Permanent fix: rebuild the image and the workspace, which then starts from the\nimage's own copy. See the next two entries for the command."],[1197,"Pin notes: grok-build-and-agents.md."],[1222,"Pin provider versions locally only if you want to, per template directory. The push\ngoes ahead either way, and `workspace` and `devcontainer` are the two names:"],[647,"Pinned as `GROK_VERSION` in `images/dev/tool-versions.env` (1.0.70 at the time of\nwriting, mirrored as the Dockerfile `ARG` default). The image build unpacks that\npinned `.zst` and runs `grok --version` in two PATH contexts as a build-time smoke\ncheck."],[37,"Pinning autostop by hand"],[690,"pins for the four auxiliary lanes - `general` and `explore` (the two subagent\ntypes) take `agent`, `compaction` and `title_generation` (the helper calls) take\n`chat` - written only for lanes that carry no pin yet, so an admin's own pins stay\nin place."],[1124,"Placeholders: `<wsid>` is a workspace id and `<ws>` a workspace name. The workspace\ncontainer is `coder-<owner>-<ws>` (so `coder-alx-self-coder`); the `<wsid>` form names\nthe DinD pieces around it - the sidecar `coder-<wsid>-dind-sidecar`, on the network\n`coder-<wsid>-dind`, with its own `coder-<wsid>-dind-lib` volume. What runs \"from the\nstack host\" needs a shell there: inside a workspace `docker` addresses that workspace's\nown private daemon through `DOCKER_HOST=tcp://dind:2375`, so a `docker inspect` aimed at\nthe stack's `coder` or `router` container and run from inside a workspace queries the\nwrong daemon and answers `no such container`. `bazelisk run //scripts:...` also runs\nfrom the checkout."],[152,"Point the CLI at the in-container plain listener, with a token by name:"],[770,"Prefer structured commands - the existing Bazel scripts and `docker compose` - over\nad-hoc shell. A script the repo owns is reviewable and test-covered; a one-liner the\nmodel invented is neither. See AGENTS.md."],[600,"Prepare the box: rotate the secrets, set `CODER_ACCESS_URL`, issue the self-signed\ncertificates, build `evo-t1-dev:latest`, pull the DinD image. It is idempotent, so re-run\nit after changing `docker-compose.yml`, `litellm/config.yaml`, `searxng/settings.yml` or\n`proxy/*.conf`."],[87,"Preset keys are parameter *names*; `display_name` is UI-only and would be ignored."],[28,"Presets"],[84,"Presets collapse the create form to one click."],[1108,"Private-repo clone or push denied while a credential is present -> the grant, not the format"],[1144,"Probe that endpoint (the card reads the same URL, `AGENT_MODEL_URL` in `.env`):"],[972,"Project conventions"],[815,"project-conventions.md is what a script has to look like to be\nmergeable, and branching.md is how it gets to `main`. The Bazel harness they\nboth assume is in the Contribute tab."],[1111,"Public `hermes-gmktecbeast` answers `421` -> no vhost, a rewritten Host, or Traefik aimed past the router"],[325,"Public hosts and the dashboard"],[1010,"Public subdomains"],[603,"Push both templates (`workspace` first, `devcontainer` last). The source travels as a tar\non stdin and the credential is minted, used and deleted in the same run, so there is no\nhost `coder` CLI and no login here:"],[1065,"Put LiteLLM behind it and every client breaks: LiteLLM authenticates from the\n`Authorization` header, and header-carried API traffic cannot pass an interactive\nsign-in. Either leave `litellm-gmktecbeast` outside any policy or add an explicit\nbypass - and then `LITELLM_MASTER_KEY` is the only credential in front of an\nendpoint that went from LAN-only to reachable WAN-wide (see\nSECURITY.md)."],[259,"Puts `~/.grok/bin` on PATH (login shells and that process)."],[1027,"Putting the five routers on the Traefik box without guessing its timeouts"],[724,"Reaching the assistant on the LAN, and on the public name when `STACK_PUBLIC_HOSTS` includes it"],[784,"Reaching the page that owns a subject from one card, instead of reading four that touch it"],[65,"Reading a failed push or a stuck workspace against what the template actually does"],[561,"Reading the box's health from one page without a shell"],[835,"Reading the routing back"],[850,"Reading the routing back, and editing an alias safely"],[823,"Reading the table"],[1199,"Rebuild the image, then rebuild the workspace; the image is fixed at create time."],[961,"Refreshing a stale checkout before diagnosing what it looks like"],[602,"Register the first account — that account is the site admin. Browsers only expose\n`crypto.randomUUID()` in a secure context, so this points at the TLS listener:"],[590,"Registering the first Coder account, pushing both templates, wiring the chat agent"],[637,"Related: coder-templates.md (the template files themselves),\nlitellm-routing.md (what the aliases route to), and\ntroubleshooting.md."],[855,"Related: coder-templates.md (the templates that render\n`~/.grok/config.toml`), grok-build-and-agents.md (the CLI and\nthe control-plane chat), project-conventions.md."],[727,"Related: dashboard.md (the card that links here),\nlitellm-routing.md (the aliases Hermes calls),\npublic-access.md (the public name, when `STACK_PUBLIC_HOSTS`